title: [+ year +]
subtitle: A new year
priority: 2
tags: event
view-if: month = 1
go-to: 1926 if year == 1926; 1927 if year == 1927; 1928 if year == 1928; 1929 if year == 1929; 1930 if year == 1930; 1931 if year == 1931; 1932 if year == 1932; 1933 if year == 1933; 1934 if year == 1934; 1935 if year == 1935; 1936 if year == 1936

= [+ year +]

@1926
on-arrival: old_republic = pro_republic; {!
// see post_event.scene.dry for changes.
Q.economic_growth -= 3;
Q.inflation -= 1;
Q.unemployed += 6;
!}

A new year begins. The economy has taken a steeply downhill turn, as unemployment shoots up across the republic. In this environment, we and the communists stand to gain.

@1927
n-arrival: old_republic = pro_republic; {!
// see post_event.scene.dry for changes.
Q.economic_growth += 5.1;
Q.unemployed -= 2;
Q.inflation -= 0.8;
if (Q.upper_tax_rates < 0) {
    Q.unemployed -= 1.1;
    Q.economic_growth += 2.5;
    Q.inflation += 0.2;
}
if (Q.lower_tax_rates < 0) {
    Q.unemployed -= 1.1;
    Q.economic_growth += 2.5;
    Q.inflation += 0.2;
}
Q.budget += 1;
!}

A new year begins. The economy is beginning to recover from the recession of the previous year, thanks in part to the attempts of stimulation by the current and previous government.

@1928
on-arrival: old_republic = pro_republic; {!
// see post_event.scene.dry for changes.
Q.economic_growth -= 5.4;
Q.inflation += 1.1;
Q.unemployed += 1.2;
Q.budget += 2;
Q.dr_exists = 0;
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    for (var c of Q.classes) {
        Q[c+'_'+party] = (Q[c+'_'+party+'_normalized']);
    } 
}
Q.thuringia_spd += 0.25; // 1.15;
Q.thuringia_uspd -= 0.3;
Q.thuringia_ddp += 0.2;
Q.thuringia_z += 0.1;
Q.thuringia_dvp -= 0.1;
Q.thuringia_dnvp -= 0.5;
Q.thuringia_other += 1.4;
Q.thuringia_nsdap += 0.1;
Q.thuringia_election_year = 1929;
Q.thuringia_election_month = 12;
!}

A new year begins. The economy continues to grow steadily, though inflation is gradually rising once more.

@1929
on-arrival: old_republic = pro_republic; {!
// see post_event.scene.dry for changes.
Q.economic_growth -= 4;

if (Q.pro_republic > 75 && Q.pro_republic > 59) {
    Q.new_middle_ddp += (Q.pro_republic - 59)
    Q.old_middle_ddp += ((Q.pro_republic - 59)/2)
    Q.new_middle_dvp += ((Q.pro_republic - 59)/2)
    Q.old_middle_dvp += (Q.pro_republic - 59)
}
!}

A new year begins. The economy appears to be slackening; unemployment is increasing throughout the republic, although for the most part, people are still doing well.
@1930
on-arrival: older_republic = old_republic; old_republic = pro_republic; {!
// increase NSDAP vote share 
Q.unemployed += 6.8; 
Q.inflation -= 4;
// historical: -1.4
Q.economic_growth -= 1;
if (Q.pro_republic > 75 && Q.pro_republic > Q.older_republic) {
    Q.new_middle_ddp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
    Q.old_middle_ddp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.new_middle_dvp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.old_middle_dvp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
}
if (Q.right_coalition_failed && Q.economic_plan) {
    Q.workers_spd += 5;
    Q.unemployed_spd += 5;
}
if (Q.budget > 0) {
    Q.budget -= 1;
}
// moved demographic changes to post_event
!}

A new year begins. The economic crisis is worsening throughout the world, with no end in sight. The NSDAP seems to be strengthening in local elections. All very worrisome trends.

@1931
on-arrival: older_republic = old_republic; old_republic = pro_republic; {!
// increase NSDAP vote share
Q.unemployed_uspd -= Q.strife;
Q.unemployed_nsdap += Q.strife; 
// TODO: if a public works program has started, unemployment is not so bad.
Q.unemployed += 6;
Q.inflation -= 5;
// historical: -7.7%
// leave some economic decline for the banking crisis event
Q.economic_growth -= 5;
if (Q.works_program) {
    Q.unemployed -= 4;
    Q.inflation += 3;
    Q.economic_growth += 3.5;
}
if (Q.works_program && Q.works_program > 1) {
    Q.unemployed -= 1.5;
    Q.inflation += 1;
    Q.economic_growth += 1.5;
}
if (Q.pro_republic > 75 && Q.pro_republic > Q.older_republic) {
    Q.new_middle_ddp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
    Q.old_middle_ddp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.new_middle_dvp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.old_middle_dvp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
}
// moved demographic changes to post_event

Q.schaumburg_lippe_nsdap += 0.6;
Q.schaumburg_lippe_dnvp += 0.05;
Q.schaumburg_lippe_spd -= 0.5;
Q.schaumburg_lippe_ddp += 25;
Q.schaumburg_lippe_dvp += 1.2;
Q.schaumburg_lippe_other -= 1;
if (Q.ddp_votes_schaumburg_lippe >= 15) {
    Q.schaumburg_lippe_ddp -= 5;
}
if (Q.ddp_votes_schaumburg_lippe < 5) {
    Q.schaumburg_lippe_ddp += 5;
}

!}

A new year begins. [? if works_program = 0 : Unemployment continues to spiral upwards. The strength of the NSDAP continues to rise. ?][? if works_program > 0 : A works program has been enacted in order to reduce unemployment. ?] [? if works_program > 0 and unemployment > 15 : However, unemployment remains too high for comfort. ?]

@1932
on-arrival: older_republic = old_republic; old_republic = pro_republic; {!
// increase NSDAP vote share 
Q.unemployed_uspd -= Q.strife;
Q.unemployed_nsdap += Q.strife;
// TODO: if a public works program has started, unemployment is not so bad.
if (Q.works_program && Q.works_program >= 2) {
    Q.unemployed -= 1;
    Q.inflation += 1;
    Q.economic_growth += 1;
}
if (Q.pro_republic > 75 && Q.pro_republic > Q.older_republic) {
    Q.new_middle_ddp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
    Q.old_middle_ddp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.new_middle_dvp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.old_middle_dvp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
}
if (!Q.works_program) {
    Q.unemployed += 5; 
    Q.inflation -= 2;
    Q.economic_growth -= 1;
}
Q.schaumburg_lippe_ddp -= 10;
Q.hamburg_ddp += 5;
if (Q.ddp_votes <= 1) {
    Q.hamburg_ddp += 15;
}
// moved demographic changes to post_event
!}

A new year begins. [? if works_program = 0 : There is little to no good news in Germany. The economic depression has still not bottomed out. ?][? if works_program >= 1 and unemployment >= 20 : We have begun to launch a public works program, but unemployment is still stubbornly high. The people are beginning to finally have optimism, however. ?][? if works_program >= 1 and unemployment < 20 : We have begun to launch a public works program, and unemployment is finally starting to fall. The people are beginning to finally have optimism. ?]

The presidential election is in April of this year.
@1933
on-arrival: nazi_decline = 1 if (nsdap_votes+unemployed < pro__republic+spd_votes); older_republic = old_republic; old_republic = pro_republic; strife += 1; {!
if (Q.pro_republic > 75 && Q.pro_republic > Q.older_republic) {
    Q.new_middle_ddp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
    Q.old_middle_ddp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.new_middle_dvp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.old_middle_dvp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
}
!}

A new year begins. [? if president == "Braun" : With Hindenburg out of office and an SPD candidate at the helm, perhaps in this year Germany will overcome its crisis. It will be our job to ensure this. ?] [? if president == "Hindenburg" : President Hindenburg's presidency continues, though for how long remains uncertain as his health deteriorates. We can only hope that should he die we may take his place and not the Nazis. ?][? if president == "Eckener" : Though Hindenburg is out of office, Hugo Eckener is by no means a social democrat. Still, matters will be easier with a staunch anti-Nazi at the helm. ?][? if president == "Gessler" : With Hindenburg out of office and Gessler at the helm, we can hope for a more liberal Germany than before. At the same time, the Bürgerblock's commitment to Brüning's economic policies pave the way for the continuation of the crisis and for someone like Hitler to take power. ?]

[? if nazi_decline = 1 : The Nazis have begun to expend their limited financial resources, and their momentum has slowed. Perhaps the far-right's moment has passed. ?]

@1934
on-arrival: older_republic = old_republic; old_republic = pro_republic; {!
if (Q.unemployed >= 20) {
    Q.unemployed -= 2;
    Q.inflation += 1;
}
if (Q.inflation < -5) {
    Q.unemployed -= 1;
    Q.inflation += 2;
}
if (Q.economic_growth > 2) {
    Q.budget += 1;
    if ((Q.upper_taxes_rates+Q.lower_tax_rates) >= 5) {
        Q.budget += 1;
        Q.economic_growth -= ((Q.upper_tax_rates+(Q.lower_tax_rates/2))/10);
    }
}
if (Q.pro_republic > 75 && Q.pro_republic > Q.older_republic) {
    Q.new_middle_ddp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
    Q.old_middle_ddp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.new_middle_dvp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.old_middle_dvp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
}
// window.dendryUI.dendryEngine.state.visits = {"1934":1}
!}

A new year begins. [? if works_program = 0 : The economic depression seems to have bottomed out, but there is still much suffering. It is not too late to launch an economic rescue program. ?][? if works_program >= 1 and unemployment >= 15 : We have begun to launch a public works program, but the economy is still troubled. The recovery has begun, but more must be done. ?][? if works_program >= 1 and unemployment < 15 : Our public works program has successfully guided us through the worst of the crisis. The economy is improving, and finally people have optimism for the future. ?]

[? if return_to_normalcy: With the return to normalcy, the political landscape in Germany is shifting. Liberalism is making a return among the middle classes, and the radical parties of the right are declining. ?]

[? if president = "Hindenburg" : The president is in poor health; he is not expected to live out the year. ?]

@1935
on-arrival: older_republic = old_republic; old_republic = pro_republic; {!
if (Q.economic_growth < 5) {
    Q.economic_growth += 0.4;
    if (Q.works_program) {
        Q.economic_growth += 1;
        Q.inflation += 0.2;
    }
    if (Q.inflation < 5) {
        Q.inflation += 0.3;
        if (Q.works_program) {
            Q.inflation += 0.2;
        }
    }
}
if (Q.unemployed >= 15 && Q.economic_growth >= 2) {
    Q.unemployed -= Q.economic_growth;
    if (Q.works_program) {
        Q.unemployed -= (Q.economic_growth/2);
    }
} else if (Q.unemployed >= 15) {
    Q.unemployed -= 2;
    if (Q.works_program) {
        Q.unemployed -= 1;
    }
} else {
    Q.economic_growth += 1;
    if (Q.works_program) {
        Q.economic_growth += 0.6;
        Q.inflation += 0.4;
    }
}
if (Q.economic_growth >= 3) {
    Q.budget += 1;
    if ((Q.upper_taxes_rates+Q.lower_tax_rates) >= 6) {
        Q.budget += 1;
        Q.economic_growth -= ((Q.upper_tax_rates+(Q.lower_tax_rates/2))/12);
    }
}
if (Q.pro_republic > 75 && Q.pro_republic > Q.older_republic) {
    Q.new_middle_ddp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
    Q.old_middle_ddp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.new_middle_dvp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.old_middle_dvp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
}
!}

A new year begins. Worldwide, the Great Depression is coming to an end, and the effects are being felt here in Germany. [? if economic_growth > 3 : The German economy is growing at an impressive pace, considering the worldwide recession. ?][? if unemployed < 15 : The unemployment rate has fallen substantially, as people across the country return to work. ?][? if inflation > 1 and inflation < 4 : Inflation is healthy, helping fuel the economy and bring down unemployment further. ?]

[? if return_to_normalcy : The Nazis have seemingly missed their window for subverting parliamentary politics and enter a period of internal reorganization. [? if sa_force + sh_force >= 50 : The threat remains, however, that they may attempt to seize power by force as a desperate last attempt at taking power. We must be vigilant. ?] ?]

@1936
on-arrival: older_republic = old_republic; old_republic = pro_republic; {!
if (Q.economic_growth < 5) {
    Q.economic_growth += 0.8;
    if (Q.works_program) {
        Q.economic_growth += 0.3;
        Q.inflation += 0.4;
    }
    if (Q.inflation < 5) {
        Q.inflation += 0.2;
        if (Q.works_program) {
            Q.inflation += 0.4;
        }
    }
}
if (Q.unemployed >= 20 && Q.economic_growth >= 3) {
    Q.unemployed -= Q.economic_growth;
    if (Q.works_program) {
        Q.unemployed -= (Q.economic_growth/2);
    }
} else if (Q.unemployed >= 20) {
    Q.unemployed -= 2;
    if (Q.works_program) {
        Q.unemployed -= 1;
    }
    if (Q.unemployed >= 25) {
        Q.unemployed -= 1;
    }
} else {
    Q.economic_growth += 0.4;
    if (Q.works_program) {
        Q.economic_growth += 0.1;
        Q.inflation += 0.2;
    }
}
if (Q.economic_growth >= 4) {
    Q.budget += 1;
    if ((Q.upper_taxes_rates+Q.lower_tax_rates) >= 7) {
        Q.budget += 1;
        Q.economic_growth -= ((Q.upper_tax_rates+(Q.lower_tax_rates/2))/14);
    }
}
if (Q.pro_republic > 75 && Q.pro_republic > Q.older_republic) {
    Q.new_middle_ddp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
    Q.old_middle_ddp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.new_middle_dvp += ((Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)/2)
    Q.old_middle_dvp += (Q.pro_republic - Q.older_republic)
}
!}

The German economy continues its steady recovery. [? if nazi_reform : The Nazis continue their reformation, attempting to seize relevance once more, but all in all, it seems that the crisis has subsided. ?][? if not third_period : Around the world, left-leaning Popular Fronts see great success, winning elections left and right. This is a good sign for our foreign policy. ?][? if budget > 0 and works_program and economic_growth >= 3 : We are running a surplus once again. It seems our works program is truly paying off. ?]

[? if italo_ethiopian_war : The Italo-Ethiopian War rages on in Abysinnia. ?]
